{"completion_ms": 859.0, "condition": "l5-query-reuse-on", "error": null, "estimated_input_tokens_for_preflight": null, "max_output_tokens_for_preflight": null, "method": "POST", "mutations": [], "path": "/api/chat", "phase": "contingency", "request_body": {"messages": [{"content": "### Task:\nRespond to the user query using the provided context, incorporating inline citations in the format [id] **only when the <source> tag includes an explicit id attribute** (e.g., <source id=\"1\">).\n\n### Guidelines:\n- If you don't know the answer, clearly state that.\n- If uncertain, ask the user for clarification.\n- Respond in the same language as the user's query.\n- If the context is unreadable or of poor quality, inform the user and provide the best possible answer.\n- If the answer isn't present in the context but you possess the knowledge, explain this to the user and provide the answer using your own understanding.\n- **Only include inline citations using [id] (e.g., [1], [2]) when the <source> tag includes an id attribute.**\n- Do not cite if the <source> tag does not contain an id attribute.\n- Do not use XML tags in your response.\n- Ensure citations are concise and directly related to the information provided.\n\n### Example of Citation:\nIf the user asks about a specific topic and the information is found in a source with a provided id attribute, the response should include the citation like in the following example:\n* \"According to the study, the proposed method increases efficiency by 20% [1].\"\n\n### Output:\nProvide a clear and direct response to the user's query, including inline citations in the format [id] only when the <source> tag with id attribute is present in the context.\n\n<context>\n<source id=\"1\" name=\"Controlled teardown corpus\" resource-type=\"collection\" resource-id=\"abc5e0a6-6b7d-4e76-ac98-821d1cc593bc\">[DOC_ID:task-model] Task model routing  \nOpen WebUI routes titles, tags, follow-up suggestions, retrieval queries, web-search queries, and autocomplete through the configured task model. Administrators can set a local or smaller task model without changing the main chat model.</source>\n<source id=\"2\" name=\"Controlled teardown corpus\" resource-type=\"collection\" resource-id=\"abc5e0a6-6b7d-4e76-ac98-821d1cc593bc\">[DOC_ID:task-cap] Task output limits  \nThe task.model.params dictionary applies generation parameters across task endpoints. A max_tokens cap therefore reaches titles and autocomplete as well as tags, follow-ups, and queries; it is not a narrow tag-only control.</source>\n<source id=\"3\" name=\"Controlled teardown corpus\" resource-type=\"collection\" resource-id=\"abc5e0a6-6b7d-4e76-ac98-821d1cc593bc\">[DOC_ID:wire-capture] Proxy evidence  \nCapture redacted provider request and response bodies, actual reported input, output, and cached tokens, completion latency, and all budget mutations. For nonstreaming task calls, mark time to first token unavailable rather than relabeling response time.</source>\n</context>\n\nAccording to the attached controlled corpus, which Open WebUI work can a smaller task model handle, and what model remains unchanged?", "role": "user"}], "model": "qwen2.5:14b-instruct", "stream": false}, "request_headers": {"Accept": "*/*", "Accept-Encoding": "gzip, deflate, br", "Content-Length": "2965", "Content-Type": "application/json", "Host": "127.0.0.1:8765", "User-Agent": "Python/3.11 aiohttp/3.13.5"}, "reservation_id": null, "response_body": {"created_at": "2026-09-15T15:22:43.8853262Z", "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "eval_count": 49, "eval_duration": 755004000, "load_duration": 1130100, "message": {"content": "According to the attached controlled corpus, a smaller task model can handle routing titles, tags, follow-up suggestions, retrieval queries, web-search queries, and autocomplete through the configured task model [1]. The main chat model remains unchanged [1].", "role": "assistant"}, "model": "qwen2.5:14b-instruct", "prompt_eval_cached_count": 